// BUG REPRO (int for entity): `Tool2::request{ input.mode: ... }` declares
// `input.mode : Drupe::Tool2_Input_mode` (an enum entity type), but the
// pattern binds it to the integer literal `5`. An int is not an entity value,
// so the field-argument type check (`check_arg_type`) should reject this with
// expected `entity:Tool2_Input_mode` vs actual `int`.
//
// The type-checker does enforce this for `==`/`!=` operands, but currently
// skips predicate `input.<field>` patterns entirely, so this validates cleanly
// when it should be rejected — a silently mis-typed field that never matches a
// real Tool2 event at runtime.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate` by the temporal type-checker.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Tool1", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tool2"::request{
        input.mode: 5
    }
};
